# WellMate Engineering Memory

This file is the persistent engineering ledger for repository changes.

## Repository baseline
- Repository: sarkarshivaditya-lab/WellMate
- Default branch: main
- Primary stack: React 19, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 7, React Router 7, Auth0, Convex, Capacitor 7, Tailwind CSS.
- Browser authentication uses Auth0; native Capacitor authentication has a dedicated callback handler.
- Convex is the backend and authenticated user records are associated through tokenIdentifier.
- Reliability architecture is documented in RELIABILITY.md.
- CI currently runs lint, TypeScript checking, deterministic emergency tests, and production build.
- Onboarding state uses localStorage keys including onboarding_profile and onboarded.

## Engineering constraints
- Do not patch symptoms while leaving duplicate or conflicting architecture behind.
- Trace callers and dependencies before structural changes.
- Preserve offline-first and recovery guarantees.
- Never edit convex/_generated manually.
- Authentication changes require end-to-end flow analysis across browser and native paths.
- Every completed code edit must be recorded below.

## Change ledger

### 2026-09-21 — Engineering foundation initialized
Status: complete
Changes:
- Added .github/skills/react-typescript-engineering.md for React/TypeScript architecture, lifecycle, typing, accessibility, and verification discipline.
- Added .github/skills/convex-engineering.md for Convex authorization, validation, idempotency, and generated-code boundaries.
- Added .github/skills/auth-and-session-engineering.md for full Auth0/OIDC/Capacitor authentication-flow analysis.
- Added .github/skills/reliability-and-safe-edits.md to preserve the repository's existing local-first, sync, hydration, and recovery contracts.
- Added .memory as the persistent change ledger.

Repository observations used to establish these skills:
- src/App.tsx owns the top-level RequireAuth route boundary and browser/native Auth0 login initiation.
- OnboardingRoute and Onboarding.tsx use localStorage-backed onboarding state.
- Convex user functions scope records through authenticated tokenIdentifier values.
- RELIABILITY.md defines the single sync path, queue behavior, recovery model, hydration state machine, and persistence contracts.

Verification:
- Repository metadata and the default branch were readable.
- Source tree and key TypeScript/auth/Convex/reliability files were audited.
- No application behavior was intentionally changed in this foundation commit.
